#N canvas 20 20 2500 1300 12;
#X text 20 20 u_init -- owns the ordered startup. loadbang fires before ALSA connections exist \, so startup is one timed sequence here rather than del objects scattered through the patch. ref/module/boot.md, f 58;
#X text 620 20 creation arg 1: the state directory \, the \$3 u_state and u_map take \; the recover breadcrumb is written there. inlets: none. outlet 1: a bang at the Launchpad stage \, to m_launchpad. outlet 2: a bang at the last stage \, to u_state \, to restore. Wires \, not sends: the stage timings are coupled to u_tempo's 4000 \, and a second file holding one of them would break that silently., f 58;
#X text 20 160 Each stage reports to disp as it is reached: a stage on screen means the sequence got that far \, not that the hardware answered., f 58;
#X declare -path ../mac-stubs;
#X obj 620 300 loadbang;
#X obj 620 340 t b b;
#X obj 620 400 del 1500;
#X obj 620 450 t b b b;
#X obj 620 540 del 1500;
#X obj 620 600 t b b b;
#X obj 620 680 del 500;
#X msg 300 360 modal booting;
#X msg 300 470 modal wiring;
#X msg 300 620 modal launchpad;
#X msg 300 770 modal-off;
#X msg 600 810 status v0.3-ready;
#X obj 140 860 s disp;
#X obj 300 720 t b b b;
#X msg 900 490 sh wire.sh;
#X obj 900 530 shell;
#X obj 900 650 outlet;
#N canvas 40 40 1120 900 panic-display 0;
#X obj 20 200 r panic;
#X msg 20 330 status panic;
#X obj 20 385 s disp;
#X text 20 620 Sticky: u_tempo bangs the BPM back out on every start and stop \, which is what clears it., f 58;
#X obj 20 260 t b b;
#X obj 300 330 t b b;
#X obj 300 440 del 1000;
#X msg 300 495 grid modal-off;
#X obj 300 550 s disp;
#X msg 560 440 grid modal 5;
#X obj 560 495 s disp;
#X text 560 620 The grid goes red (palette 5) \, and the del's modal-off is the point: leaning on g_grid's 30 s safety TTL would take the grid away when it is most needed. No ownership is touched (C-5 \, item 251)., f 58;
#X connect 0 0 4 0;
#X connect 4 0 1 0;
#X connect 4 1 5 0;
#X connect 5 1 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X restore 900 760 pd panic-display;
#X text 140 920 Stage timings are guesses with evidence: the 1500 ms is item 266 (ref/module/boot.md). If the Launchpad comes up unlit \, lengthen the second delay before suspecting the SysEx., f 58;
#X text 620 920 wire.sh runs from /tmp/patch \, Pd's working directory on the device. Each aconnect may fail without stopping the rest., f 46;
#X text 1080 920 shell exists only on the Organelle \; mac-stubs/shell.pd stands in for it in the syntax check., f 46;
#X obj 900 570 print wire;
#X text 140 1050 The stages are modals \, taking the whole screen. The last sends modal-off and puts v0.3-ready in the footer., f 58;
#X text 620 1050 A message box typed modal booting already has modal as its selector. C-6, f 46;
#X text 1080 1050 The footer is handed over: u_tempo drops the BPM in at 4 s \, after v0.3-ready lands at 3.5 s. Change these timings and that 4000 changes with them., f 40;
#X obj 1180 240 loadbang;
#X msg 1180 375 0;
#X obj 1180 420 s midiInGate;
#X text 1550 240 mother's own MIDI mapping goes off first: its omni ctlin 21 to 26 collide with the nano's top row \, and a program change loads another patch (Reference \, critter-guitari-organelle-1)., f 44;
#X obj 1180 285 t b b;
#X obj 1320 330 del 2000;
#X text 1550 680 Sent twice: the mother binary pushes its own midiInGate 1 about half a second in \, so the 2 s copy is the one that works (ref/module/boot.md)., f 44;
#X obj 1350 420 s midiOutGate;
#X text 1550 900 midiOutGate 0: mother echoes the keys and knobs to every output port \, lighting Launchpad pads and firing 404 pads. Our own midiout is untouched., f 50;
