#X text 1180 620 The Launchpad stage is an outlet: this file decides when \, and m_launchpad how., f 44;
#X obj 1180 850 outlet;
#X text 2000 680 Restore at the last stage \, 3.5 s in \, the earliest moment every m_ layer and u_map can receive it \, and first of the three so the screen settles after the state., f 44;
#X text 2000 1060 Outlets are numbered by x position (Reference \, pure-data) \, so this one stays right of the Launchpad outlet., f 44;
#N canvas 40 40 1400 1250 recover 0;
#X text 20 20 Panic's second tier: recover reloads the patch \, which re-enumerates every device. That is the only recovery for a device nothing can detect \, like the Volca (item 275) \, and for a wedged patch., f 62;
#X obj 20 300 r recover;
#X obj 20 350 t b b b b;
#X obj 900 350 realtime;
#X obj 900 300 loadbang;
#X obj 900 420 list prepend recover;
#X obj 900 530 text define \$0-crumb;
#X obj 900 475 text set \$0-crumb 0;
#X obj 520 420 symbol \$1;
#X msg 520 475 write -c \$1/cut-it-recover.txt;
#X obj 300 420 s panic;
#X obj 20 420 del 300;
#X msg 20 475 sh recover.sh;
#X obj 20 530 shell;
#X text 20 620 Right to left \, all four ordered: the breadcrumb first \, since after the reload nothing is left to write it \; then panic \, so killing Pd leaves no stuck note \; then 300 ms for the silence to reach the wire., f 62;
#X text 20 860 A fork on an event \, within the rule's terms: rare \, one per gesture (u_map's del 2000 bounds it) \, and it ends the patch \, so nothing can cascade behind it., f 62;
#X text 900 620 The stamp is milliseconds since load \, enough to tell one attempt from another in the log., f 44;
#X text 900 860 shell's outlet goes nowhere: oscsend is fire and forget \, and the patch that would read a reply is about to be killed (ref/module/map.md)., f 44;
